.git/
.gitignore
*.vsix

# --- development-only material: keep it out of the published package ---------
# The runtime needs: extension.js, debug_adapter.js, resolver.cjs, mcp/**,
# templates/**, images/**, syntaxes/**, language-configuration.json, package.json,
# README.md, CHANGELOG.md, LICENSE, and TROUBLESHOOTING.md (opened by the
# "Troubleshooting & Written Guide" command, so it MUST ship).
.claude/
.vscode/
review/
test/

# Internal notes and specs.
#
# SELF-SUFFICIENCY RULE: the package must contain everything the shipped docs link to. An installed
# extension may be a different version from the repo, and may be offline, so a link that resolves to
# a file outside the package is either dead or silently showing DIFFERENT content. Consequences:
#   - docs/** ships (the "Manual" command opens docs/README.md)
#   - TROUBLESHOOTING.md ships (opened by "Troubleshooting & Written Guide")
#   - CORE-CONCEPTS.md ships (8 KB, linked from the docs index)
#   - images/** ships, screenshots included, and README images use RELATIVE paths
# Before excluding anything here, check nothing in README.md or docs/** links to it.
DOGFOODING.md
DESIGN-*.md
SPEC-*.md

# NOTE: images/screenshots/ MUST ship. The README links them with RELATIVE paths, and VS Code
# renders the extension's details page from the INSTALLED FOLDER — an absolute raw.githubusercontent
# URL showed a broken icon there (and 404s until the file is pushed). vsce rewrites the relative
# links to https for the Marketplace page, so relative works in all three places at the cost of
# carrying the PNGs in the package.

# Editor/OS noise
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
*.log
